      {
        "id": 85747,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-14T20:01:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Lets keep things within some semblance of perspective here. The online comic is a suppliment for the card game and its lore, not the other way around. With that said, measuring its worth against Marvel/DC books is not exactly a fair comparison when their purpose and focus is much different. It gave life and personality to otherwise unknown static character faces printed on card stock. In that regard it was quite a successful suppliment which happened to use the narrative form that the game tries to emulate.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:31.237Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
